/.claude/worktrees
.env
scripts/jira/dist/
# where-are-we ledger L2 (HIMMEL-516): regenerated-from-live-sources cache, not
# source of truth — never commit it.
/.where-are-we/
# node_modules anywhere — none are tracked. A per-package list let
# marketplace/plugins/*/node_modules/ slip through and be sweepable (HIMMEL-371).
node_modules/
/.claude/settings.local.json
# tokensave MCP code-graph state (local SQLite DB, session-generated — never commit).
/.tokensave/
# graphify knowledge-graph artifacts (HIMMEL-621, REMOVED HIMMEL-2705 step 1
# from the git tree entirely — this repo's derived graph no longer PUBLISHES
# at all). Formerly (HIMMEL-1123) the two portable artifacts (graph.json,
# GRAPH_REPORT.md) were tracked so stations that can't afford the LLM-backed
# extraction (win2: "no resources") could pull them instead of re-extracting.
# That cross-station-pull design is retired: the directory is now ignored
# OUTRIGHT, nothing re-included. Working files stay on disk — the daily
# HIMMEL-829 cadence keeps rebuilding them locally, and every place that
# used to COMMIT or PR the graph now no-ops on this ignored path instead.
graphify-out/*
# .claudeignore
# Claude Code prompt cache invalidated after every graphify extract Graphify writes output files (graph.json, graphify-out/) into the workspace. If those paths aren't ignored, every write invalidates Claude Code's prompt cache, forcing a full re-upload at cache-write rates on the next turn. Add them to .claudeignore:
graph.json
graphify-out/
/.claude/skills/graphify/
# graphify multi-harness init scatters per-machine integration files across the
# repo (HIMMEL-1193). Regenerable via /graphify, same as the ignored skills dir
# above; `.gemini/settings.json` also embeds an absolute local graphify.exe path
# (per-machine, HIMMEL-1134/1168 leak class) so it can't be committed as-is.
# Shipping graphify multi-harness support portably is HIMMEL-1194.
.gemini/
/.github/copilot-instructions.md
.agents/rules/graphify.md
.agents/workflows/graphify.md
# Generated/junk artifacts that must never be committed (HIMMEL-371).
# NOT package-lock.json globally — 6 legit npm packages track theirs. The
# wrong-PM lockfile case (a package-lock.json inside a bun package, left by the
# npm-audit pre-push gates) is prevented per-bun-package via that package's own
# .gitignore (e.g. marketplace/plugins/luna-correlate/, scripts/luna-vitals/),
# and still backstopped by the check-artifact-leakage pre-commit hook.
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# stray empty scratch file at the repo root — not produced by any himmel script
# (HIMMEL-1193); anchored so it only ignores the root stray.
/.tmp
# end-session-wiki hook local artifacts — contain raw transcript excerpts (potential secrets).
# Match any .claude/ dir (the hook writes into the cwd's .claude/, e.g. scripts/telegram/.claude/).
**/.claude/end-session-wiki.log
**/.claude/end-session-wiki.log.old
# run-hook-with-bash.js --chain durable skip/deny log (HIMMEL-2060) — local
# diagnostics, not source. Not root-anchored (CR round 4, codex-2): the
# launcher falls back to cwd when CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is unset, so a nested
# invocation writes .claude/logs/ under a subdirectory too.
**/.claude/logs/
# Handover transient state
.last-consolidate.json
**/handovers/*/.last-consolidate.json
.pending-new-item*
**/handovers/*/.pending-new-item*
.pending-consolidate*
**/handovers/*/.pending-consolidate*
# auto-arm-on-cap / auto-arm-on-subagent-cap runtime snapshots (HIMMEL-276) —
# the hooks write these into himmel handovers/ as untracked clutter on main.
# (Followup: redirect the hook write path to HANDOVER_DIR — see HIMMEL ticket.)
handovers/auto-arm-status-*.md
# arm-resume lock files (arms.jsonl) — transient arming-lock state that lands in
# the himmel handovers/ stub as untracked clutter; observed staged on main
# (HIMMEL-1024), same class as the auto-arm-status snapshots above.
handovers/.locks/
# Overnight-mode reports/recovery artifacts — auto-generated session state
# (morning-report.sh et al.) that belongs in the state repo, not the himmel
# handovers/ stub. Archived copies live in <state-repo> handovers/yotamleo/himmel/.
handovers/overnight-report-*.md
handovers/overnight-recovery-*.md
# Cross-project handover content moved to <state-repo> in HIMMEL-13 —
# prevent accidental re-tracking if the operator's local copy still
# exists or gets re-created here by an out-of-date tool.
/handovers/luna/
/handovers/manual_notes.md
/handovers/random_dreams.md
# Runtime artifacts that pollute primary-worktree git status
.claire/
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# HIMMEL-1552: the settings writers' exclusive lock. Transient, but it sits
# beside a TRACKED file, so a crash-orphaned one would otherwise be swept up by
# `git add -A`.
/.claude/settings.json.lock
/.playwright-mcp
# /improve disk artifacts — Mode A inline path. Mode B writes under HANDOVER_DIR.
/.improve/
# /gemini-bg background-run output sink (HIMMEL-158)
logs/gemini/
# superpowers design docs were removed for OSS (HIMMEL-297); overnight-mode
# Mode A (no HANDOVER_DIR) regenerates plans under docs/superpowers/plans/ —
# keep those local, never re-track the folder into the public repo.
/docs/superpowers/
# Internal design/plan/decision specs belong in the luna state repo, never in
# himmel docs/ (HIMMEL-409). himmel docs/ is reference + OSS-public only. Ignore
# docs/specs/ so migrated-out specs can't silently re-track (and never leak to
# the public mirror). New specs go to <state-repo>/handovers/<user>/<repo>/specs/.
/docs/specs/
# Decision records (ADRs) are state-repo work artifacts too (HIMMEL-409) —
# they belong in <state-repo>/.../specs/decision/, never himmel docs/.
/docs/adr/
# Codex artifacts (HIMMEL-427: codex IS now wired). The guardrail wiring is
# TRACKED (hooks.json + the platform run-hook wrappers + its README); codex's local
# runtime config, sessions, and auto-generated slash-command→skill mirrors stay
# ignored. (AGENTS.md itself is tracked separately.)
.codex/*
!.codex/hooks.json
!.codex/run-hook.cmd
!.codex/run-hook.sh
!.codex/codex-hook-adapter.sh
!.codex/README.md
.agents/skills/source-command-*/
# himmel-contributor marker (opt-in; enables doc-guard gate) — never commit it
.himmel-dev
# per-operator CR registry overlay (account quota state) — never commit (HIMMEL-727)
scripts/cr/critics.local.json
# per-machine lane availability/override overlay (himmelctl config) — never commit (HIMMEL-758)
scripts/lanes/lanes.local.json
# machine-local grok tool-schema cache dir — never commit (HIMMEL-876)
/mcps/
# scripts/lanes/bench/runs/ (HIMMEL-2560, REMOVED HIMMEL-2705 step 1): bench
# RUN-OUTPUT JSONs moved to the luna state repo — the bench tooling still
# writes fresh runs here locally, so the directory stays gitignored instead
# of tracked. See scripts/lib/public-clone-paths.sh for the move rationale.
scripts/lanes/bench/runs/
# stray Corsair iCUE/CorsairLink driver log dropped in the repo root by the
# host tooling — machine-local noise, never ours to commit (HIMMEL-1611).
CorsairLink.log
# CPython bytecode for the harness's tracked .py sources — pure build
# byproducts, regenerated on the next import, never work product (HIMMEL-2584).
# Left untracked-but-unignored, they read to clean-garden as "untracked files
# that are not known strays (possible forgotten work)", so it correctly refuses
# to prune — and EVERY merged worktree became unprunable (5 of 5 on this
# station). The guard's verdict was right; the repo had just never told git
# these files are noise.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
